      "notes": "Section 1.2.1.6 'Rhotics, Final and Otherwise' (p. 7): ⟨ர⟩ is 'a phonetically flapped or tapped r, more or less alveolar' and 'does not undergo gemination (doubling)'; ⟨ற⟩ 'was originally an alveolar stop', is trilled intervocalically, and geminates. Section 1.2, item 4 (p. 14) describes medial single stops as 'laxed and fricativized', with the palatal and velar 'only laxed but not usually voiced'."
